From: Zizheng Guo <gzz_2000@126.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tgsi_to_nir: read an input FACE as TGSI's float

TGSI's FACE is a float, positive of front faces, where shaders read it from
an input, and an integer, ~0 of front faces, where they read it from a
system value. tgsi_to_nir gave a driver whose face is an integer system
value, as Zink's is, the integer of either: an input FACE of a front face
was ~0, a NaN, which Mesa's virgl driver, which reads its FACE from an
input, compares with 0.0, and so took for a back face. It now gives each
file its own, of either face of the driver.

